# Search results pagination

As a user, I want to page through search results so I can browse more than the first page of matches.

* the catalog has more than one page of results

## Navigating to the next page
Tags: search, pagination

* the user has performed a search that returns more than one page of results
* the user clicks the "Next" pagination control
* the second page of results replaces the first page
* the pagination control shows page 2 as active

## Jumping to a specific page
Tags: search, pagination

* the user has performed a search that returns more than one page of results
* the user clicks the page <page> control
* the <page> page of results replaces the current page
|page|
|2|
|3|
